{title: Who Is a God Like You}
{subtitle: Micah 7:1–9; 7:18–20}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
What misery is mine, gathering fruit af[Bb]ter harvest
Like gleaning the vineyard when [Gm]the grapes are gone
[Bb]Not a cluster left to eat, not one early [Dm]fig
The faithful have vanished [C]from the land entire[Dm]ly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Not one upright person remains among us
They all [Bb]lie in wait for blood in the dark
[Gm]Each one hunts his own brother with a net
[Bb]Both hands are skilled [C]at weaving evil [Dm]tight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The [Bb]official demands his price, [C]the judge takes his bribe
[Dm]The powerful dictate what they want to do
[Bb]The best is like a briar, [C]a hedge of thorns
[Gm]Confusion falls upon them all today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Who is [Dm]a God like you, [C]who pardons guilt
Pass[Bb]ing over the transgression of [Gm]his remnant
You [Dm]do not hold on to [C]your anger forever
[Bb]For you delight [C]in mercy, yes [Dm]you do
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Put no trust in a neighbor or a friend
[Bb]Guard your mouth even from the wife in [Gm]your arms
A son treats his father with contempt
[Bb]A daughter rises [C]against her mother [Dm]now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
En[Bb]emies are the members [C]of my own house[Dm]hold
Trust is broken and the bonds are torn
[Bb]But as for me, I [C]will look to the LORD
I [Gm]will wait for the God of my salvation
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Who is [Dm]a God like you, [C]who pardons guilt
[Bb]Passing over the transgression [Gm]of his remnant
You [Dm]do not hold on to [C]your anger forever
[Bb]For you delight [C]in mercy, yes [Dm]you do
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Do not [C]gloat over me, my [Dm]enemy [Bb][C][Dm]
Though I [Bb]sit in darkness, [C]the LORD is my [Gm]light
I will bear his wrath until he hears me
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You will [Bb]hurl all our [C]sins into the [Dm]depths of the sea
You will [Bb]show faithful[C]ness to Jacob and [Dm]Abraham
{end_of_verse}
